  "schema:name": "NanoSIMS O isotopic analysis of precursor silicates in sample OREX-501059-0",
  "schema:description": "Small oliivne, pyrovene and other silicate and oxide phases exist within the matrix of Bennu samples. These phases are the remnants of the precursor components that formed the original Bennu parent asteroid. The oxygen isotopic composititon of these grains helps constrain the nature of what Bennus parent formed from, and where in the protoplanetary disk this happened.",
